term	0	15	15	en	0	<p>A formal request to merge your changes into the original project or the main branch. It lets other developers review the code (Code Review) before it is approved.</p>	basic_html
term	0	16	16	en	0	<p>Push uploads your commits from your computer to the remote server. Pull downloads updates made by others from the server to your computer.</p>	basic_html
term	0	17	17	en	0	<p>A central storage location that holds all the files, code and change history of a project.</p>	basic_html
term	0	18	18	en	0	<p>A Linux command that shuffles or randomly selects lines. Example: shuf -e {A..Z} -n 1 picks one random uppercase letter from A to Z.</p>	basic_html
term	0	19	19	en	0	<p>A program that provides a text interface (CLI) for communicating with the operating system. It is used to run commands, scripts and programs.</p>	basic_html
